  <section class="section">
    <h2>Abstract</h2>

    <p>
      Dual Brain Robotics Architecture (DBRA) is a bilateral
      robotic control system inspired by the dual-hemispheric
      structure of the human brain.
    </p>

    <p>
      Unlike conventional robotic systems that rely upon a
      single centralized processing pathway, DBRA employs
      two coordinated processing modules that continuously
      exchange perceptual, predictive, and error-correction
      information.
    </p>

    <p>
      Through reciprocal monitoring and coordinated action
      mapping, the architecture seeks to improve robotic
      stability, balance, dexterity, adaptive behavior,
      micromotor precision, and fluid movement in dynamic
      environments.
    </p>

    <p>
      The architecture represents the first patent-pending
      application derived from concepts developed in
      <em>Closer to Consciousness</em> (Durig, 2023).
    </p>
  </section>

