  <section class="section">
    <h2>Research Foundation</h2>

    <p>
      Dual Brain Robotics Architecture™ is grounded in
      concepts introduced in Alexander Durig's theory of
      consciousness and perception.
    </p>

    <p>
      The architecture explores whether principles associated
      with bilateral cognition may provide a foundation for
      more adaptive robotic perception and motor control.
    </p>

    <p>
      Interested readers may also wish to review
      <em>Closer to Consciousness: The First Strong Theory of Consciousness</em>
      and related research materials presented elsewhere on
      this website.
    </p>

  </section>

